{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QW4bskYX973oWKh3aAwG8p","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Checkpoint Criterion Analysis: best_by_val_loss vs best_by_R@1\n2\t\n3\t**Date**: 2026-05-15\n4\t**Purpose**: Ablation material for paper — analyze dual checkpoint selection divergence and K=7 rationale.\n5\t\n6\t## 1. Dual Checkpoint Mechanism\n7\t\n8\tThe training script (`training/train.py`) maintains two independent best checkpoints:\n9\t- **best_by_val_loss**: Updated when `val_loss < best_val_loss` (also drives early stopping)\n10\t- **best_by_recall_at_1**: Updated when `R@1 > best_R@1` (independent of early stopping)\n11\t\n12\tBoth are evaluated at `eval_steps=500` intervals. The final eval at training end does NOT update either checkpoint.\n13\t\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t## 2. Full M2 Runs — Checkpoint Alignment Table\n17\t\n18\t| Run | Encoder | Strategy | Seed | best_by_val_loss | best_by_R@1 | Aligned? | R@1 gap | Evidence |\n19\t|-----|---------|----------|------|-----------------|-------------|----------|---------|----------|\n20\t| m2_full_qwen | Qwen2.5-Coder-3B | random | 42 | step 1000 (vl=0.4651, R@1=0.5527) | step 1000 (R@1=0.5527) | **Yes** | 0pp | timestamps 35s apart |\n21\t| m2_full_qwen | Qwen2.5-Coder-3B | random | 43 | step 500 (vl=0.4476, R@1=0.5357) | step 1500 (R@1=0.5554) | **No** | +1.97pp | timestamps 4.12h apart |\n22\t| m2_full_qwen | Qwen2.5-Coder-3B | random | 44 | step 500 (vl=0.4252, R@1=0.6009) | step 500 (R@1=0.6009) | **Yes** | 0pp | timestamps 6s apart |\n23\t| m2_full_starcoder | StarCoder2-3B | random | 42 | step 1000 (vl=0.6134, R@1=0.454) | step 2500 (R@1=0.4604) | **No** | +0.64pp | timestamps 8.34h apart |\n24\t\n25\t### Full eval trajectory for diverged runs\n26\t\n27\t**Qwen random_s43** (early stopped at step 1500):\n28\t\n29\t| Step | val_loss | R@1 | best_by_val_loss? | best_by_R@1? |\n30\t|------|----------|-----|-------------------|--------------|\n31\t| 500 | **0.4476** | 0.5357 | **Yes** (saved) | Yes (first) |\n32\t| 1000 | 0.4637 | 0.5285 | No (↑ vs 0.4476) | No (↓ vs 0.5357) |\n33\t| 1500 | ? | **0.5554** | No (early stop triggered) | **Yes** (saved) |\n34\t\n35\tval_loss and R@1 diverge: val_loss selects the less-overfit step 500, R@1 selects the better-ranking step 1500.\n36\t\n37\t**StarCoder random_s42** (3 full epochs):\n38\t\n39\t| Step | val_loss | R@1 | best_by_val_loss? | best_by_R@1? |\n40\t|------|----------|-----|-------------------|--------------|\n41\t| 500 | 0.6194 | 0.435 | Yes (first) | Yes (first) |\n42\t| 1000 | **0.6134** | 0.454 | **Yes** (saved) | Yes (saved) |\n43\t| 1500 | 0.6528 | 0.449 | No | No |\n44\t| 2000 | 0.6698 | 0.4456 | No | No |\n45\t| 2500 | 0.6342 | **0.4604** | No | **Yes** (saved) |\n46\t| 3000 | 0.6516 | 0.4544 | No | No |\n47\t| 3500 | 0.6588 | 0.4534 | No | No |\n48\t| 4000 | 0.6637 | 0.4547 | No | No |\n49\t\n50\tStarCoder shows a dramatic divergence: val_loss overfits immediately after step 1000, but R@1 continues improving until step 2500 — 1500 steps (and 8+ hours) later.\n51\t\n52\t---\n53\t\n54\t## 3. Pilot Runs (24 repos) — Checkpoint Alignment\n55\t\n56\t| Encoder | Strategy | Seed | best_by_val_loss | best_by_R@1 | Aligned? |\n57\t|---------|----------|------|-----------------|-------------|----------|\n58\t| Qwen | random | 42 | step 500 (vl=0.4834) | step 500 (R@1=0.5357) | **Yes** |\n59\t| Qwen | embedding | 42 | step 500 (vl=0.4603) | step 500 (R@1=0.5557) | **Yes** |\n60\t| Qwen | dataflow | 42 | step 500 (vl=0.5602) | step 500 (R@1=0.5436) | **Yes** |\n61\t| SC2 | embedding | 42 | step 1000 (vl=0.4816) | step 1000 (R@1=0.5078)* | **Yes** |\n62\t| SC2 | dataflow | 42 | step 1000 (vl=0.5255) | step 1000 (R@1=0.4869)* | **Yes** |\n63\t\n64\t*Note: pilot runs only had 2 eval points (step 500, 1000) before training ended. Final eval (R@1=0.5174 for embedding, 0.5078 for dataflow) was higher than step 1000 but does NOT update best_by_R@1 checkpoints per code logic. Fewer eval points make alignment more likely by chance.\n65\t\n66\t---\n67\t\n68\t## 4. Alignment Rate Summary\n69\t\n70\t### Full M2 runs (completed, with 3+ eval points):\n71\t- **2 / 4 aligned = 50%**\n72\t\n73\t### All runs including pilots:\n74\t- **7 / 9 aligned = 78%**\n75\t- But pilot alignment is inflated due to only 2 eval points\n76\t\n77\t### Pattern observed:\n78\t- **Qwen tends to align** (2/3 full runs = 67%), likely because Qwen's pretrained representations have very high cosine similarity ceiling (pos_sim=0.985), so overfitting and R@1 degradation track together\n79\t- **StarCoder tends to diverge** (0/1 full run, but 1500-step gap is extreme), likely because StarCoder's wider margin (2.6-4.1x Qwen) gives the model more room to improve ranking after the loss curve inflects\n80\t\n81\t---\n82\t\n83\t## 5. Recommendation: Which Criterion to Report\n84\t\n85\t### Primary: Report best_by_R@1\n86\t- R@1 is the target metric; val_loss is a proxy\n87\t- When diverged, best_by_R@1 always gives equal or better R@1 (by definition)\n88\t- The R@1 gap when diverged is meaningful: +1.97pp (Qwen s43), +0.64pp (SC2 s42)\n89\t- Reporting val_loss-selected checkpoint would understate performance by up to ~2pp\n90\t\n91\t### Secondary: Report both in ablation\n92\tPresent a \"checkpoint criterion ablation\" table showing:\n93\t\n94\t| Run | R@1 (best_by_R@1) | R@1 (best_by_val_loss) | Delta |\n95\t|-----|-------------------|----------------------|-------|\n96\t| Qwen random_s42 | 0.5527 | 0.5527 | 0pp |\n97\t| Qwen random_s43 | 0.5554 | 0.5357 | +1.97pp |\n98\t| Qwen random_s44 | 0.6009 | 0.6009 | 0pp |\n99\t| SC2 random_s42 | 0.4604 | 0.454 | +0.64pp |\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4036345-91c5-47f2-9c09-36d0f1b82314","uuid":"95af9c92-e660-4899-b825-372e8cf1d470","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:16:55.327Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/structfuse-context/artifacts/_project/report/checkpoint_criterion_analysis.md","content":"# Checkpoint Criterion Analysis: best_by_val_loss vs best_by_R@1\n\n**Date**: 2026-05-15\n**Purpose**: Ablation material for paper — analyze dual checkpoint selection divergence and K=7 rationale.\n\n## 1. Dual Checkpoint Mechanism\n\nThe training script (`training/train.py`) maintains two independent best checkpoints:\n- **best_by_val_loss**: Updated when `val_loss < best_val_loss` (also drives early stopping)\n- **best_by_recall_at_1**: Updated when `R@1 > best_R@1` (independent of early stopping)\n\nBoth are evaluated at `eval_steps=500` intervals. The final eval at training end does NOT update either checkpoint.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Full M2 Runs — Checkpoint Alignment Table\n\n| Run | Encoder | Strategy | Seed | best_by_val_loss | best_by_R@1 | Aligned? | R@1 gap | Evidence |\n|-----|---------|----------|------|-----------------|-------------|----------|---------|----------|\n| m2_full_qwen | Qwen2.5-Coder-3B | random | 42 | step 1000 (vl=0.4651, R@1=0.5527) | step 1000 (R@1=0.5527) | **Yes** | 0pp | timestamps 35s apart |\n| m2_full_qwen | Qwen2.5-Coder-3B | random | 43 | step 500 (vl=0.4476, R@1=0.5357) | step 1500 (R@1=0.5554) | **No** | +1.97pp | timestamps 4.12h apart |\n| m2_full_qwen | Qwen2.5-Coder-3B | random | 44 | step 500 (vl=0.4252, R@1=0.6009) | step 500 (R@1=0.6009) | **Yes** | 0pp | timestamps 6s apart |\n| m2_full_starcoder | StarCoder2-3B | random | 42 | step 1000 (vl=0.6134, R@1=0.454) | step 2500 (R@1=0.4604) | **No** | +0.64pp | timestamps 8.34h apart |\n\n### Full eval trajectory for diverged runs\n\n**Qwen random_s43** (early stopped at step 1500):\n\n| Step | val_loss | R@1 | best_by_val_loss? | best_by_R@1? |\n|------|----------|-----|-------------------|--------------|\n| 500 | **0.4476** | 0.5357 | **Yes** (saved) | Yes (first) |\n| 1000 | 0.4637 | 0.5285 | No (↑ vs 0.4476) | No (↓ vs 0.5357) |\n| 1500 | ? | **0.5554** | No (early stop triggered) | **Yes** (saved) |\n\nval_loss and R@1 diverge: val_loss selects the less-overfit step 500, R@1 selects the better-ranking step 1500.\n\n**StarCoder random_s42** (3 full epochs):\n\n| Step | val_loss | R@1 | best_by_val_loss? | best_by_R@1? |\n|------|----------|-----|-------------------|--------------|\n| 500 | 0.6194 | 0.435 | Yes (first) | Yes (first) |\n| 1000 | **0.6134** | 0.454 | **Yes** (saved) | Yes (saved) |\n| 1500 | 0.6528 | 0.449 | No | No |\n| 2000 | 0.6698 | 0.4456 | No | No |\n| 2500 | 0.6342 | **0.4604** | No | **Yes** (saved) |\n| 3000 | 0.6516 | 0.4544 | No | No |\n| 3500 | 0.6588 | 0.4534 | No | No |\n| 4000 | 0.6637 | 0.4547 | No | No |\n\nStarCoder shows a dramatic divergence: val_loss overfits immediately after step 1000, but R@1 continues improving until step 2500 — 1500 steps (and 8+ hours) later.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Pilot Runs (24 repos) — Checkpoint Alignment\n\n| Encoder | Strategy | Seed | best_by_val_loss | best_by_R@1 | Aligned? |\n|---------|----------|------|-----------------|-------------|----------|\n| Qwen | random | 42 | step 500 (vl=0.4834) | step 500 (R@1=0.5357) | **Yes** |\n| Qwen | embedding | 42 | step 500 (vl=0.4603) | step 500 (R@1=0.5557) | **Yes** |\n| Qwen | dataflow | 42 | step 500 (vl=0.5602) | step 500 (R@1=0.5436) | **Yes** |\n| SC2 | embedding | 42 | step 1000 (vl=0.4816) | step 1000 (R@1=0.5078)* | **Yes** |\n| SC2 | dataflow | 42 | step 1000 (vl=0.5255) | step 1000 (R@1=0.4869)* | **Yes** |\n\n*Note: pilot runs only had 2 eval points (step 500, 1000) before training ended. Final eval (R@1=0.5174 for embedding, 0.5078 for dataflow) was higher than step 1000 but does NOT update best_by_R@1 checkpoints per code logic. Fewer eval points make alignment more likely by chance.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Alignment Rate Summary\n\n### Full M2 runs (completed, with 3+ eval points):\n- **2 / 4 aligned = 50%**\n\n### All runs including pilots:\n- **7 / 9 aligned = 78%**\n- But pilot alignment is inflated due to only 2 eval points\n\n### Pattern observed:\n- **Qwen tends to align** (2/3 full runs = 67%), likely because Qwen's pretrained representations have very high cosine similarity ceiling (pos_sim=0.985), so overfitting and R@1 degradation track together\n- **StarCoder tends to diverge** (0/1 full run, but 1500-step gap is extreme), likely because StarCoder's wider margin (2.6-4.1x Qwen) gives the model more room to improve ranking after the loss curve inflects\n\n---\n\n## 5. Recommendation: Which Criterion to Report\n\n### Primary: Report best_by_R@1\n- R@1 is the target metric; val_loss is a proxy\n- When diverged, best_by_R@1 always gives equal or better R@1 (by definition)\n- The R@1 gap when diverged is meaningful: +1.97pp (Qwen s43), +0.64pp (SC2 s42)\n- Reporting val_loss-selected checkpoint would understate performance by up to ~2pp\n\n### Secondary: Report both in ablation\nPresent a \"checkpoint criterion ablation\" table showing:\n\n| Run | R@1 (best_by_R@1) | R@1 (best_by_val_loss) | Delta |\n|-----|-------------------|----------------------|-------|\n| Qwen random_s42 | 0.5527 | 0.5527 | 0pp |\n| Qwen random_s43 | 0.5554 | 0.5357 | +1.97pp |\n| Qwen random_s44 | 0.6009 | 0.6009 | 0pp |\n| SC2 random_s42 | 0.4604 | 0.454 | +0.64pp |\n","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":173}}}
